                    rdfs:subClassOf pmat:SamplePreparation ;
                    rdfs:comment "Controlled increase of pressure during supercritical drying to bring the drying fluid above its critical point, typically performed at controlled ramp rate"@en ;
                    skos:definition "A sample preparation step in which pressure is increased in a controlled manner, in supercritical drying bringing the drying fluid above its critical point"@en ;
                    rdfs:label "Pressurization"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/polymat/Procedure
pmat:Procedure rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000003 ,
                               prov:Entity ;
               rdfs:comment "An executed procedure consisting of a set of activities carried out as the accepted way of doing something. This class denotes the occurrent that unfolds in time, not the recipe/plan that prescribes it — for the latter, see gmat:SynthesisProtocol. Axioms deliberately match Polymat 1.1.0 (BFO occurrent + prov:Entity) so that resolving the owl:imports of Polymat does not introduce conflicting redeclarations. Note: Procedure is placed under BFO occurrent (BFO_0000003) rather than BFO process (BFO_0000015) because Polymat maps BFO_0000015 to prov:Activity, which PROV-O declares disjoint from prov:Entity."@en ;
               rdfs:label "Procedure"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol
gmat:SynthesisProtocol rdf:type owl:Class ;
                       rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000031 ;
                       rdfs:comment "A plan specification (recipe/protocol) that prescribes how a sol-gel synthesis is to be carried out. As a generically dependent continuant it is the reusable, copyable information artifact that a concrete synthesis process (an occurrent) realises. Distinguishes the recipe from any individual run of it."@en ;
                       skos:definition "A generically dependent continuant that is an information artifact prescribing the ordered activities, materials, and conditions for carrying out a sol-gel synthesis; realised by one or more concrete synthesis processes."@en ;
                       rdfs:label "Synthesis protocol"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter
gmat:ProcessParameter rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000019 ,
                                      om:Quantity ;
                      rdfs:comment "A quality (in the BFO sense) that characterises the material inputs or setup of a synthesis process — e.g. a molar or volume ratio of reagents, a pH condition, or a stirring rate. Modelled as a quality that inheres in an independent continuant (typically the reacting mixture / sol), carrying its numeric magnitude via an om:Measure. Achieved, per-run values (not plan prescriptions). Also a subclass of om:Quantity (itself under pmat:Feature), so that process parameters can carry values via om:hasValue and satisfy the pmat:Feature domain of pmat:isParameterOf."@en ;
                      skos:definition "A quality inhering in an independent continuant that characterises the material inputs or setup of a synthesis process, recording an achieved per-run value"@en ;
                      rdfs:label "Process parameter"@en .


